    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the full test suite is green (2/2 tests passing, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nDELETE `/api/owners/{id}` now soft-deletes owners instead of removing the row. Changes made:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()` (defaults to `false` for new owners).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 two small edits in existing methods:\n   - `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and calls `saveOwner` (retaining the row, still returning `204`) instead of `deleteOwner`.\n   - `addOwner` filters `deleted` owners out of `existingOwners`, so the duplicate/identity/household checks ignore soft-deleted records \u2014 a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match is deleted.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `deleted` property to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct maps it automatically by name, so `GET` returns `deleted` (`false` before, `true` after deletion).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column and updated the seed inserts to match (the positional `INSERT`s require the extra value).\n\n### On structural impact\nI kept each touched function simple and localized: the entity change is a plain field plus two one-line accessors; both controller edits are minimal in-place changes to existing methods rather than new branching logic. I limited the DB changes to the **hsqldb** schema \u2014 the complete, test-active one (`ddl-auto=none`). The h2/postgres/mysql schemas are already stale relative to the entity (each is missing `postcode`, `household_id`, `namesake_count`, and other columns), so I did not touch them; doing so would add files without making any real path correct.",
